UPDATE companies SET description='Tomahawk Manufacturing Inc was founded in 1992 in Plymouth, Wisconsin. The company began with a mission to provide the food processing industry with an alternative source for spare parts, tooling, and equipment at competitive prices while maintaining high standards of ethics and integrity.

The company designs and manufactures a line of food forming machines — the TM-26, TM-19, TM-400, and TM-6 — capable of throughputs from 1,200 to 6,000 pounds per hour. It also produces custom tooling in-house, supplies spare parts, and provides engineering, field service, training, and automation integration through its Industrial Control Associates division in Albany, Georgia. Operations span a corporate headquarters and manufacturing site in Plymouth, an engineering office in Hartland, Wisconsin, and a European subsidiary in Rijswijk, Netherlands.

Tomahawk serves beef, poultry, seafood, pork, plant-based protein, pet food, and pet pharmaceutical processors worldwide. Its equipment forms products such as beef patties, chicken nuggets, fish cakes, sausages, plant-based proteins, pet treats, and pharmaceutical pills. Customers range from large-scale protein processors to specialty pet treat manufacturers across North America, South America, Europe, and Asia.

The company emphasizes responsive, customer-first support, including 24/7 emergency assistance, on-site service, and comprehensive training programs. Its founding vision — to deliver uncompromising quality and service at competitive rates while maintaining a personal connection with each customer — continues to guide its global operations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food forming equipment manufacturing", "Custom tooling design and manufacturing", "Spare parts supply", "Field service and on-site support", "Engineering and design", "Automation and control systems integration", "Training programs", "Tooling audits"], "industries": ["Beef processing", "Poultry processing", "Seafood processing", "Pork processing", "Plant-based protein processing", "Pet food processing", "Pet pharmaceutical processing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["TM-26 Food Forming Machine", "TM-19 Food Forming Machine", "TM-400 Food Forming Machine", "TM-6 Food Forming Machine"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Alternative source for former spare parts, tooling, and equipment at competitive prices", "Global presence with offices in Plymouth, WI and Rijswijk, Netherlands", "24/7 emergency assistance and on-site field service worldwide", "In-house custom tooling design and manufacturing", "Comprehensive operator training programs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 -> /", "Headquarters Plymouth, WI -> /about", "Global offices in Plymouth, Hartland, Albany, Netherlands -> /about", "TM series machines with throughput specs -> /", "Industries served: beef, poultry, seafood, pork, plant-based, pet food, pet pharmaceutical -> /", "Services: engineering, field service, customer support, training -> /services", "Mission, vision, values -> /about", "In-house tooling, spare parts, forming equipment -> /", "Industrial Control Associates (ICA) automation integration -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence"