UPDATE companies SET description='Tomfoolery Wood Co. operates from Kent, Washington, in the Pacific Northwest. The company handcrafts custom solid wood furniture in a Seattle-area workshop, building each piece from start to finish.

The shop produces armoires, benches, bookcases, consoles, dressers, vinyl LP storage units, and tables using more than six native Pacific Northwest hardwoods — including Willamette walnut, white oak, maple, cherry, madrone, and myrtle. Wood is hand-selected from responsibly forested sources, with some salvaged from orchards and urban trees at end of life. The team employs waste-minimizing processes and offers custom stain finishes along with solid brass or wood hardware.

The company serves residential clients and design professionals seeking heirloom-quality furniture.

Tomfoolery Wood Co. emphasizes sustainability and intentional design, partnering with regional mills and restoration projects to give salvaged wood a second life. The collaborative design process aims to create furniture that tells a story and lasts generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom solid wood furniture design", "Handcrafted manufacturing", "Hand selection of hardwood", "Waste-minimizing processes", "Custom stain finishing", "Hardware installation (solid brass or wood pulls)", "Height adjustable shelves", "Salvaged wood sourcing"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Custom furniture", "Interior design"], "materials": ["Willamette walnut", "White oak", "Maple", "Cherry", "Madrone", "Myrtle", "Salvaged Willamette Valley walnut", "Solid brass"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Approximately 8-12 weeks to start production; ~17 weeks to order fulfillment", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Waste-minimizing production processes", "Responsibly forested and salvaged Pacific Northwest hardwoods", "Handcrafted from start to finish in a Seattle-area workshop", "Custom stain finishes and solid brass or wood hardware options", "Collaborative design process for bespoke pieces"], "facts_used": ["Location: Kent, Washington -> db", "Handcrafted in Pacific Northwest -> /", "Custom solid wood furniture design/manufacturing -> /", "Lead time ~17 weeks to fulfillment -> /", "Lead time 8-12 weeks to start production -> products (db)", "More than six local wood species native to PNW -> /", "Wood species: Willamette walnut, white oak, maple, cherry, madrone, myrtle -> /about", "Salvaged Willamette Valley walnut from orchards and urban trees -> /about", "Responsibly forested hardwood -> /about", "Waste-minimizing processes -> /about", "Hand select every piece of hardwood, build start to finish in Seattle workshop -> /about", "Custom stain options, premium hardware (solid brass or wood pulls) -> /about", "Height adjustable shelves -> products (db)", "Collaborative design process -> /about", "Serves residential clients and design professionals -> /about", "Testimonials from customers in Seattle, Portland, Missouri -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Solid Wood Furniture Design/Manufacturing", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tomfoolery-wood-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tonka Electronics, Inc. was founded on September 1, 1976 in Bloomington, Minnesota as a manufacturer''s representative and stocking distributor for the printed circuit board fabrication and assembly industry. The woman-owned small business was incorporated in Minnesota by founder Mike DeLadi, who emphasized a "no slogans, just service" philosophy. Initially focused on representing capital equipment lines, the company expanded into stocking consumables required by that equipment.

Today Tonka operates as a focused distributor specializing in soldering and cleaning products, maintaining a fully stocked warehouse of leaded and lead-free solder bar, wire, and paste, along with fluxes, flux additives, solder masks, and cleaning agents. The company also offers its own SpliceRite line of SMT tape splicing products, cover tape extenders, and carrier tape cutting tools, plus SmartDry intelligent dry storage systems for SMT component reels and trays. Services include manufacturability assessment, process design, technical training, solder analysis, and low-cost resharpening. Tonka supplies spare parts and accessories for Electrovert equipment such as spray fluxers, convection preheaters, chip waves, and nitrogen nozzles, and provides test solutions for Ionograph and OmegaMeter ionic contamination testers.

The company serves the printed circuit board fabrication and assembly sector across its manufacturer''s representative territory of Minnesota, North and South Dakota, northwest Wisconsin, and occasionally Iowa. As a distributor, it ships nationwide to electronics manufacturers, including medical device producers who use fine hard wire cutting tools. Customers range from contract manufacturers to OEMs implementing new production lines.

Tonka differentiates itself through deep technical expertise in soldering and cleaning processes, offering both equipment integration support and a broad inventory of consumables available for immediate shipment. The founder''s service-first approach remains central, with the company providing free samples of SpliceRite products and hands-on assistance with process development.', certifications=ARRAY['Woman-owned']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Manufacturer''s representative for PCB fabrication and assembly equipment", "Stocking distributor for soldering and cleaning consumables", "Capital equipment sales and integration support", "Process development assistance", "Leaded and lead-free solder distribution (bar, wire, paste)", "Flux, flux additive, solder mask, and cleaning agent supply", "SMT tape splicing products (SpliceRite line)", "Cover tape extenders and carrier tape cutting tools", "Manufacturability assessment", "Process design and technical training", "Intelligent dry storage systems for SMT components (SmartDry)", "Spare parts for Electrovert equipment (spray fluxers, convection preheaters, chip waves, nitrogen nozzles)", "Ionic contamination testing solutions (Ionograph, OmegaMeter)", "Solder analysis services", "Specialty coating systems", "Low-cost tool resharpening services", "SMT placement equipment lines", "Portable wave and oven optimizers with SPC (OvenRIDER)", "24-hour continuous product quality monitoring (OvenWATCH)"], "industries": ["Printed circuit board fabrication and assembly", "Electronics manufacturing", "Medical device manufacturing"], "materials": ["Leaded solder (bar, wire, paste)", "Lead-free solder (bar, wire, paste)", "Fluxes", "Flux additives", "Solder masks", "Cleaning agents"], "equipment": ["Electrovert equipment (spray fluxers, convection preheaters, chip waves, nitrogen nozzles)", "Ionograph ionic contamination testers", "OmegaMeter ionic contamination testers", "OvenRIDER portable wave and oven optimizers", "OvenWATCH continuous monitoring systems", "SpliceRite SMT tape splicing tools", "SmartDry intelligent dry storage systems", "SMT placement equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Woman-owned small business founded in 1976", "Focused distributor specializing in soldering and cleaning products", "Fully stocked warehouse with leaded and lead-free solder bar, wire, and paste", "Nationwide shipping as a distributor; regional manufacturer''s representative territory", "Free samples of proprietary SpliceRite SMT tape splicing products"], "facts_used": ["Founded September 1, 1976 as Manufacturer''s Representative and stocking Distributor -> /", "Woman-owned, small business incorporated in Minnesota -> /", "Headquarters Bloomington, Minnesota -> /", "Founder Mike DeLadi mentioned -> /", "Territory as manufacturer''s representative: MN, ND, SD, NW WI, sometimes IA -> /", "Distributor territory not limited geographically -> /", "Specializes in soldering and cleaning products -> /", "Stocks leaded and lead-free solder bar, wire, paste, fluxes, additives, masks, cleaning agents -> /", "SpliceRite SMT tape splicing products, cover tape extenders, carrier tape cutting tools -> /", "SmartDry intelligent dry storage systems for SMT components -> /", "Services: manufacturability assessment, process design, technical training, solder analysis, resharpening -> /", "Spare parts for Electrovert equipment (spray fluxers, convection preheaters, chip waves, nitrogen nozzles) -> /", "Test solutions for Ionograph and OmegaMeter ionic contamination testers -> /", "OvenRIDER portable wave/oven optimizers with SPC -> /", "OvenWATCH 24-hour continuous product quality monitoring -> /", "Serves PCB fabrication and assembly industry -> /", "Medical industry mentioned for fine hard wire cutting tools -> /", "Certification: Woman-owned -> db", "Capabilities list from database -> db", "Products list from database -> db", "Industries served from database -> db"], "company_type"