UPDATE companies SET description='Torque King 4x4 operates from Billings, Montana, where it supplies 4x4 truck parts and tools to individual owners and commercial fleets. The business began as QUAD 4x4 before adopting its current name, though a founding year is not publicly disclosed. Dan Guarino serves as vice president and appears in the company''s technical videos and media appearances.

The company functions as a manufacturer, a stocking distributor of original-equipment parts, and an exporter. Its catalog spans 4x4 special tools, genuine OEM components, aftermarket parts, and service kits for vehicles dating from 1941 to current models. Coverage includes Dana-Spicer axles (models 25 through 80), Ford Sterling axles, AAM axles, New Process/New Venture transfer cases, NV4500 and NV5600 transmissions, Getrag G360 transmissions, and related driveshaft components. Torque King also produces color-illustrated shop manuals and technical service bulletins, and maintains a library of video guides such as the Mahindra Roxor front hub service.

The company emphasizes support for work trucks used on highways, job sites, gravel roads, and ranchland. Brands carried include Timken bearings, Dana axle components, Morse chains, and National seals, alongside Torque King''s own power-train line.

Torque King positions itself around domestic manufacturing and supply-chain resiliency. In a televised segment on Viewpoint with Dennis Quaid, Guarino discussed reshoring and the balance between domestic and foreign sourcing in the truck-parts sector. The firm highlights its ability to stock hard-to-find small parts essential for quality repairs and its technical content from "Dan the Gear Man."', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Manufacturing of 4x4 power train components", "OEM parts distribution", "Export of 4x4 parts and tools", "Technical publication (shop manuals, service bulletins)", "Video-based maintenance guides", "Technical support and parts selection assistance", "Curated selection of aftermarket and OEM components", "Fleet and individual customer parts fulfillment"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Commercial fleet maintenance", "Off-road/4x4 vehicle service", "Construction equipment support", "Agricultural/ranch vehicle support"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Manufacturer, OEM parts distributor, and exporter under one roof", "Publishes illustrated shop manuals and technical service bulletins for 4x4 vehicles", "Stocks extensive hard-to-find small parts for Dana, Ford Sterling, AAM, and New Venture drivelines", "Produces video maintenance guides and technical articles by in-house expert Dan the Gear Man", "Advocates for U.S. manufacturing reshoring in the truck-parts supply chain"], "facts_used": ["Location: Billings, Montana -> db", "Formerly QUAD 4x4 -> /about-us", "Manufacturer, OEM parts distributor, exporter -> /about-us", "Publishes shop manuals and technical service bulletins -> /about-us", "Dan Guarino is Vice President -> /", "Covers 4x4 vehicles from 1941 to present -> /about-us", "Carries brands: Timken, Dana, Morse, National Seals -> /about-us", "Offers video guides for maintenance -> /", "Appeared on Viewpoint with Dennis Quaid -> /", "Serves personal truck owners and fleets -> /", "Focus on USA-backed parts and reshoring -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Torque King 4x4 (formerly QUAD 4x4) is a Montana USA based manufacturer, stocking OEM parts distributor, and exporter of a large selection of 4x4 special tools, genuine original equipment parts, quality aftermarket parts, and service kits", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='torque-king-4x4' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tova Industries LLC was founded in 1985 in Jeffersontown, Kentucky, as a manufacturer, packer, and distributor of dry food products.

The company produces a range of dry food items, including clean-label products, whole-wheat offerings, and nutrient-enhanced lines high in protein and fiber. Its portfolio includes the Tova Farms brand and the Carbquik Bake Mix, sold through carbquik.com. Operations cover custom formulation, proprietary process development, high-protein mix and drink production, plant-based complete meals, and natural flavor and color conversion.

