iance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tova-industries-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tower Metal Works Inc. was founded in 1976 by Howard Willsey in a garage in Maple Hill, Kansas. The family-owned business grew from that modest start into a 50,000-square-foot facility, expanding its building and services over decades while retaining its original family values.

Today the company operates as a full-service sheet metal fabrication shop, offering laser cutting, punching, press brake forming, CNC machining, welding (MIG, TIG, and spot), 3D scanning, plating, prototyping, and engineering support. Its equipment roster includes two Amada laser cutters (one a 9,000 kW ENSIS fiber laser with automated material loading), a 4,500 kW laser/punch combination, five Amada HG2204 press brakes capable of 172-inch bends, and a HURCO VMX 6030i machining center holding ±0.001-inch tolerance. The shop serves customers nationwide from its single Kansas location.

Tower Metal Works serves a broad base of industrial clients requiring precision metal parts, from prototype runs to higher-volume production. The company emphasizes minimizing outsourcing to keep turnaround times short, and it provides free quotes that are typically returned the next business day.

The firm cites its family-oriented culture, investment in Amada’s latest fiber-laser technology, and a team of highly qualified welders as key differentiators. By keeping capabilities in-house—from cutting and forming to machining and finishing—it aims to deliver consistent quality and faster delivery than competitors who rely on subcontractors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting", "Punching", "Press brake forming", "CNC machining (drilling, milling, chamfering, tapping, countersinking)", "Welding (MIG, TIG, spot welding)", "3D scanning", "Plating", "Prototyping", "3D modeling", "Engineering support", "Pem setting", "Shearing", "Sawing", "Etching"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Amada ENSIS 9,000 kW Fiber Optics Laser", "Amada laser cutting machines (2)", "4,500 kW Laser/Punch Combo", "Amada HG2204 Press Brake (5)", "HURCO VMX 6030i machining center"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.001 in (HURCO VMX 6030i)", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1976 with retained family values", "50,000 sq ft facility enabling in-house capabilities to reduce outsourcing", "Amada ENSIS 9,000 kW fiber laser with automated material loader", "Free quotes typically returned next business day", "Five Amada press brakes for forming up to 172 inches"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1976 by Howard Willsey in a garage -> /about", "Facility covers 50,000 sq ft -> /about", "Family values retained -> /about", "Services nationwide -> /about", "Full-service sheet metal fabrication shop -> /about", "Laser cutting with two Amada machines, including ENSIS 9,000 kW fiber laser -> /services", "Punching up to 10 gauge steel, 58 turret station -> /services", "Five Amada HG2204 press brakes, max 172 in, 220 tons -> /services", "HURCO VMX 6030i machining center, tolerance \u00b10.001 -> /services", "Welding: MIG, TIG, spot welding -> /services", "Materials: carbon steel, stainless stee