Toyota Boshoku states that its development process is founded in human factors and ergonomics, aiming to create seats that support a comfortable driving posture, adapt to body variations, and reduce fatigue on long drives. The company emphasizes lightweight materials such as expanded kenaf base material and technologies like one-motor power seats to differentiate its offerings.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Simultaneous back-injection molding", "Fine hold stamping", "Foam in place method", "Product engineering", "Production engineering", "Testing and evaluation engineering", "Driving simulator operation", "Proving ground testing", "Lightweight molded foam door trim production", "Expanded kenaf base material processing", "One-motor power seat assembly", "Hydrogen power system integration"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Aerospace", "Commercial seating"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Driving simulator", "Proving ground", "Development equipment and facilities"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Development process based on human factors and ergonomics", "Simultaneous back-injection molding technology", "Fine hold stamping method", "Lightweight molded foam door trim with high impact resistance", "Expanded kenaf base material for sustainable components"], "facts_used": ["Harrodsburg, Kentucky location -> db", "Development process founded in human factors and ergonomics -> db", "Simultaneous Back-Injection Molding Technology -> db", "Fine Hold Stamping Method -> db", "Product categories: Seats, Interior & Exterior, Unit Components, Filter Products, Plastic Parts for ICE, Products for Electric Vehicles, Textile Components -> pages", "Aircraft seats mentioned -> pages", "Foam In Place Method -> pages", "Lightweight Molded Foam Door Trim with High Impact Resistance -> pages", "Expanded Kenaf Base Material -> pages", "One-Motor Power Seats -> pages", "Hydrogen power system -> pages", "Driving Simulator -> pages"