UPDATE companies SET description='Troy Brook Visions operates from a red barn studio and gallery on Clark Road in Litchfield, Connecticut. The company was founded in 1993 by Daniel Gugnoni, a sculptor turned furniture maker, who established the business on the Shaker principles of hard work, honesty, and pride in craftsmanship. Barbara Gugnoni joined the venture in 1996, bringing a background in advertising and sales to manage client relations and the finishing process.

The studio produces one-of-a-kind and custom fine art furniture, each piece designed and handcrafted by Daniel Gugnoni. The work emphasizes pure forms and clean lines, allowing the natural character of each wood board to guide the design. Barbara applies a twelve-step hand-rubbed finish to protect and enhance the surfaces. The operation is deliberately small-scale, with no mass production; the barn houses both the workshop and a second-floor gallery where completed pieces are displayed.

Troy Brook Visions serves private clients seeking heirloom-quality furniture, as well as collectors and visitors who attend the gallery or the craft shows where the company exhibits. The firm has shown at the American Craft Council Shows, the Paradise City Arts Festival, the Philadelphia Invitational Furniture Show, the Fine Furnishings Show, and Crafts America. Clients work directly with Daniel on custom commissions, while the gallery offers ready-made pieces for immediate purchase.

The company distinguishes itself by rejecting volume manufacturing in favor of artistic creation, a philosophy captured in the statement "Never manufacturing product, always creating art." The Shaker-inspired founding ethos and the practice of letting the wood dictate the form remain central to the studio''s identity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted woodworking", "Hand-rubbed finishing (twelve-step process)", "Custom joinery", "Art furniture design"], "industries": ["Fine art furniture", "Custom woodworking", "Art and craft exhibitions"], "materials": ["Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only one-of-a-kind and custom pieces; no mass production", "Twelve-step hand-rubbed finishing process", "Direct collaboration with master artisan Daniel Gugnoni on every commission", "Red barn studio and gallery in historic Litchfield Hills", "Exhibitor at major juried craft shows including American Craft Council"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1993 -> /about-us", "Founder Daniel Gugnoni -> /about-us", "Barbara Gugnoni joined in 1996 -> /about-us", "Location: Litchfield, Connecticut -> db", "Red barn studio and gallery -> /", "One-of-a-kind custom pieces only -> /", "Twelve-step hand-rubbed finish -> /about-us", "Direct client collaboration with Daniel -> /about-us", "Participation in American Craft Council Shows, Paradise City Arts Festival, Philadelphia Invitational Furniture Show, Fine Furnishings Show, Crafts America -> /about-us", "Shaker philosophy of hard work, honesty, pride in craftsmanship -> /about-us", "Artist statement: ''Never manufacturing product, always creating art'' -> /", "Materials: wood -> /", "Company type: Manufacturer -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Master Artisan Daniel Gugnoni designs and creates exquisite custom handcrafted fine art furniture.", "founded_year": "1993", "employee_count":