UPDATE companies SET description='Turntech was founded in April 2002 by Curvin and Lucille Horning in Ephrata, Pennsylvania.

Today, Turntech produces a wide range of custom wood turnings, including columns, porch posts, mouldings, kitchen island legs, balls, and dowels. The team can replicate historic profiles through reeding, rope twisting, barley twisting, and fluting, and accepts customer-provided photos, sketches, or CAD drawings for made-to-order projects.

The company has supplied half a dozen porch columns for a historic restoration and recreated a lyre for a Duncan Phyfe chair, demonstrating its ability to handle both architectural and decorative commissions.

Turntech emphasizes domestic production, shipping custom orders in as little as five business days, and the ability to match existing designs exactly. The founders highlight a blend of old-world craftsmanship with modern technology, a commitment to employing local craftsmen, and community involvement in Lancaster County.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC wood turning", "Custom wood manufacturing", "Wood column turning (reeding, rope twist, barley twist, fluting)", "Porch post manufacturing", "Custom turning design and manufacture", "Moulding production (crown, base, corner, chair rail, hand rail, rope mouldings)", "Kitchen island leg manufacturing", "Wooden ball and dowel production", "Historic restoration matching", "Design from photos, sketches, or CAD drawings"], "industries": ["Home renovation", "Historic restoration", "Construction/contracting", "Furniture manufacturing", "Stairway manufacturing", "Arts and crafts", "Martial arts equipment", "Kitchen and bath", "Architectural millwork"], "materials": ["Walnut", "Cherry", "Mahogany", "Maple", "Oak", "Cedar", "Pine", "Poplar"], "equipment": ["Custom CNC lathe (up to 17.5\" round, 144\" long)", "Hydraulic copy lathe"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "As little as 5 business days", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Made in the USA", "Custom made-to-order options", "Ships in as little as 5 business days", "Matches existing designs from photos or CAD", "Combines old-world craftsmanship with CNC technology"], "facts_used": ["Founded April 2002 by Curvin & Lucille Horning -> db", "Started in 2-car garage with hydraulic copy lathe -> db", "Headquartered in Ephrata, Pennsylvania -> db", "Custom CNC lathe capacity: 17.5\" round, 144\" long -> /", "Wood species: walnut, cherry, mahogany, maple, oak, cedar, pine, poplar -> /", "Products: columns, porch posts, mouldings, island legs, balls, dowels -> /", "Lead time: as little as 5 business days -> /", "Made in USA, custom made-to-order, matches exis