UPDATE companies SET description='Ullmer''s Dairy Equipment & Fabrication operates from Pulaski, Wisconsin, where Francis Ullmer founded the business in 1991 with a single bulk tank sold from his front yard. The family-owned company grew into a 10-acre inventory of used cheese-making equipment in Northeast Wisconsin before Francis passed leadership to his son Paul after 22 years. Paul added a fabrication shop to produce food-grade stainless steel equipment built to individual customer specifications.

Today the shop combines a skilled design team with experienced fabricators to deliver custom stainless steel tanks, vats, pasteurizers, presses, and conveyors for sanitary processing. The facility also refurbishes and resells used dairy machinery, maintaining a large stock of batch pasteurizers, cheese vats, CIP systems, and related accessories. In-house engineering supports both one-off prototypes and repeat production runs.

Its equipment also reaches wineries, breweries, maple syrup producers, honey operations, and educational institutions that require food-grade fabrication.

