UPDATE companies SET description='Unified Medical Equipment Solutions operates from Jacksonville, Arkansas, with additional clinics in Bentonville, Jonesboro, and Newport. The company’s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed. It began as a provider of orthotic, prosthetic, durable medical equipment, and respiratory services across northern Arkansas.

The company delivers clinical services and custom-fabricated devices. Its clinical team provides orthotic services such as functional foot orthotics, ankle-foot orthoses, spinal orthoses, and cranial remolding helmets. Prosthetic services include post-operative care, transtibial and transfemoral prostheses, and partial foot devices. The durable medical equipment lineup spans walkers, hospital beds, CPAP/BiPAP units, wheelchairs, oxygen concentrators, and negative-pressure wound therapy systems. Custom design and fabrication is offered for orthotic and prosthetic devices.

UMES serves patients, caregivers, and healthcare providers throughout northern Arkansas. Its customer base includes amputees, individuals with mobility impairments, and those requiring respiratory support.

